+</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We read the fee pages of the five managers serving Horry County that print their long-term fees. A long-term rental is a home leased to one tenant for a year or more. Three of the five have an office in Horry County. Firm C serves Myrtle Beach from its Charleston office, in Summerville. Firm D is the Myrtle Beach rentals site of a national brokerage's local franchise, and it prints no office address.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:49.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>What five managers serving Horry County print for a yearly lease, main plan</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Manager</th><th scope="col">Each month</th><th scope="col">To find a tenant</th><th scope="col">Renewal</th><th scope="col">Setup</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Firm A: North Myrtle Beach office, full-service plan</th><td data-label="Each month">10% of the rent</td><td data-label="To find a tenant">One month's rent</td><td data-label="Renewal">$150</td><td data-label="Setup">None</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Firm B: Myrtle Beach office, standard plan</th><td data-label="Each month">10% of the rent</td><td data-label="To find a tenant">45% of a month's rent</td><td data-label="Renewal">$100</td><td data-label="Setup">$200</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Firm C: regional firm, full-service plan</th><td data-label="Each month">10% of the rent</td><td data-label="To find a tenant">Half a month's rent</td><td data-label="Renewal">Not printed</td><td data-label="Setup">Not printed</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Firm D: a brokerage's Myrtle Beach rentals site</th><td data-label="Each month">10% of the rent, if collected</td><td data-label="To find a tenant">One month's rent</td><td data-label="Renewal">Not printed</td><td data-label="Setup">Not printed</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Firm E: Myrtle Beach office, flat-fee plan</th><td data-label="Each month">As low as 7%, $150 minimum</td><td data-label="To find a tenant">None</td><td data-label="Renewal">Not printed</td><td data-label="Setup">Not printed</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fee to find a tenant is called a leasing or placement fee. It runs from nothing to one full month's rent, and half a month is the middle. A renewal fee is charged when the tenant signs on for another year. The two firms that print one charge $100 or $150.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Compare dollars, not percents. A plan that prints "as low as 7 percent" with a $150 monthly minimum costs about 9 percent on a $1,600 rent. $150 is more than 7 percent of any rent under about $2,140.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="a-year"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Cost in a year">What does a property manager cost in a year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fee to find a tenant changes the total from one year to the next. We worked out a year of fees on a <span style="white-space:nowrap">3-bedroom</span> house renting for $1,600 a month, on the terms in the table above.</p><div class="pm-ex" role="group" aria-label="Worked example"><p class="k" style="margin-top:0">Worked example: a <span style="white-space:nowrap">3-bedroom</span> house renting for $1,600 a month</p><dl><div><dt>The manager's 10 percent</dt><dd>$160 a month, $1,920 a year</dd></div><div><dt>A year with a new tenant<span class="s">Add half a month's rent to place the tenant. Or a full month's rent, at the firm that then starts its 10 percent in the second month.</span></dt><dd>about $2,700 to $3,400</dd></div><div><dt>A year the tenant stays<span class="s">Add a $100 to $150 renewal fee.</span></dt><dd>about $2,050</dd></div><div class="t"><dt>Most years, with a new tenant about 1 year in 4</dt><dd>about $2,200 to $2,400</dd></div></dl><p>That is about 12 percent of the rent, not 10.</p></div><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>Why 1 year in 4.</strong> About 1 in 4 households renting a house here moved in within the past 12 months.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>What it leaves out.</strong> Repairs, and the <a href="#extra-fees" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">charges on top</a> that some firms print.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What a house rents for here, by bedrooms and area, is on our <a href="/invest/rent-prices/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rent prices page</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want this worked out for the house you are looking at?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We put the manager's fee next to the rent, tax, insurance and HOA dues. You see whether the rent still covers the costs.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us run this house</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="vacation-rentals"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Vacation rentals">What does a vacation rental manager charge in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">More than a long-term manager, because there is more work. A vacation rental, also called a short-term rental, is rented by the night or the week. Owners here pay for one of two kinds of plan:</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>What owners here pay a vacation rental manager, in the rentals we have seen</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">The manager takes</th><th scope="col">What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Basic plan</th><td data-label="The manager takes">About 13 to 17% of the bookings</td><td data-label="What it covers">Marketing, guest messages, bookkeeping</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Full service</th><td data-label="The manager takes">About 40 to 60% of profit after costs</td><td data-label="What it covers">Basic, plus taxes and repairs</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On a basic plan, you still arrange the cleaning, and repairs and tax help cost extra. Full service is a share of what is left after the costs of running the home. Its dollar cost depends on those costs.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Local firms that print a vacation rental fee show 10 to 25 percent of the booking. One Little River firm prints 15 percent and charges cleaning to the guests, not the owner. We plan with the ranges above, which come from rentals we have seen run.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The average Myrtle Beach vacation rental listing, of any type or size, takes in about $25,800 a year in bookings. That counts the cleaning fees guests pay. On all of it, 13 percent is about $3,400 and 17 percent is about $4,400.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-10-d/invest-str-vs-ltr/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-from-the-beach-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-10-d/invest-str-vs-ltr/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-from-the-beach-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-10-d/invest-str-vs-ltr/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-from-the-beach-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 680px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Tall oceanfront towers with rows of balconies behind the dune in Myrtle Beach, with more towers lined up along the beach into the distance under a blue sky" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: DiscoA340. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: DiscoA340</a></span></div><figcaption>Oceanfront towers along the beach in Myrtle Beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether nightly guests beat a yearly lease is on our <a href="/invest/str-vs-ltr/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term against long-term rental page</a>. A condo in a building with its own rental program is weighed on <a href="/invest/rental-program-vs-airbnb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental program or Airbnb</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Buying a condo with a rental program?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">We read the owner-use and exit terms of the building's program agreement with you before you sign.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us read the program terms</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="do-you-need-one"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Do you need one">Do I need a property manager, or can I manage it myself?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A manager is the person near the home who shows it, lets in repair people and answers the tenant. Of the homes here that are not anyone's main home, about 6 in 10 have a tax bill mailed outside the area.</p><figure class="c3-gchart"><div role="table" aria-label="For most rentals and second homes here, the tax bill goes outside the area"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">For most rentals and second homes here, the tax bill goes outside the area</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Tax bill mailed to, homes</span><span role="columnheader">share</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Inside the area</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 37,500 homes</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.946" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">37%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Elsewhere in South Carolina</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 7,400 homes</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.186" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">7%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Carolina</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 17,200 homes</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.434" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">17%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Other states</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 39,700 homes</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">39%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Outside the U.S.</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 600 homes</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.016" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">under 1%</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Horry County homes not taxed as anyone's main home: rentals, second homes and others. &quot;Inside the area&quot; means Horry County's post-office ZIP codes and Pawleys Island's.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Carolina gets the most of these bills. After it, for houses, come New York, Pennsylvania, Virginia and New Jersey.</p><p class="pm-cap">Do you need a property manager?</p><ul class="pm-rules" role="list" aria-label="Do you need a property manager?"><li><p class="t">A house on a yearly lease, and you live away</p><p><strong>Hire a manager.</strong> Someone near the home has to let in the tenant and the repair people.</p></li><li><p class="t">A house on a yearly lease, and you live here</p><p><strong>Run it yourself, or hire a manager.</strong> You need no license to rent out your own home.</p></li><li><p class="t">A condo in an oceanfront building</p><p><strong>Compare the building's rental program with a manager.</strong> About 8 in 10 oceanfront condos for sale list a vacation rental program.</p></li><li><p class="t">A vacation rental on a booking site</p><p><strong>Hire a full-service manager, or take the basic plan and your own cleaner.</strong> The worst mistake we see is running it yourself with the cheapest cleaner. Theft and damage have followed.</p></li></ul><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:560px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/invest-property-management/key-in-a-lockbox-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/invest-property-management/key-in-a-lockbox-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/invest-property-management/key-in-a-lockbox-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 680px) 100vw, 560px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A brass house key hanging inside an open gray combination lockbox" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Brainy J. License: CC0" title="License: CC0">Photo: Brainy J</a></span></div><figcaption>A key in a lockbox. When you live away, someone near has to let in the tenant, the plumber and the next showing.</figcaption></figure><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Looking for a manager here?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Once we are working together, we introduce you to the management companies we recommend.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us which managers we recommend</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="extra-fees"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Fees on top">What do property managers charge besides the monthly fee?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For the monthly share, a long-term manager advertises the home, screens applicants and signs the lease. The manager also collects the rent and arranges repairs. Federal fair housing law applies to the advertising, the screening and the lease. The five fee pages also print charges on top of it, and a few things they leave out:</p><ul class="pm-rules" role="list"><li><p class="t">A setup fee</p><p>Firm B charges $200 to start. Firm A prints no setup fee.</p></li><li><p class="t">A month with no rent</p><p>Firm D takes its fee only on rent it collects. The other four pages do not say what they charge in a month no rent comes in.</p></li><li><p class="t">Inspections</p><p>Firm B's standard plan includes the move-in and move-out inspections. It charges $100 for an extra inspection you ask for.</p></li><li><p class="t">Repairs</p><p>Firm B usually pays repair bills up front and takes them out of your next month's payment. You may use your own repair person. None of the five pages prints a markup on repair bills.</p></li><li><p class="t">Evictions</p><p>Many managers handle evictions, depending on the plan. Most charge their percentage of the rent whatever the work, but some bill an eviction by the hour. Firm E charges no eviction fee beyond the cost of serving the papers and the court's costs.</p></li><li><p class="t">A tenant who leaves early</p><p>If a tenant Firm D placed breaks the lease in the first 12 months, Firm D finds a new tenant for free.</p></li></ul><figure class="pm-flow" role="group" aria-label="How the money moves on a long-term rental with a manager"><ol><li><b><span>1</span>The tenant pays</b>The rent each month, and a security deposit at the start.</li><li><b><span>2</span>The manager's trust account</b>A bank account for other people's money. The deposit stays in it until the lease ends.</li><li><b><span>3</span>You are paid</b>The rent, after the bank clears it, less the manager's fee.</li></ol><figcaption>How the money moves on a long-term rental with a manager. Our own drawing.</figcaption></figure><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Have a management agreement in front of you?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send it to us before you sign. We read the fee lines, the renewal pay and the way out with you.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us the agreement</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="taxes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Rental taxes">Who pays the taxes on a vacation rental in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On stays under 90 days, whoever takes the guest's booking and payment collects the state's 7 percent accommodations tax on the full booking. That is the manager or the booking site, or you when you book the guest yourself.</p><table class="pm-tab"><caption>On a stay under 90 days, what the guest pays</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">The charge</th><th scope="col">Taxed?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The nightly rent</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>A cleaning fee every guest must pay</td><td>Yes, like the rent</td></tr><tr><td>A cleaning fee the guest can choose to skip</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three more rules for a vacation rental owner:</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>A state retail license.</strong> An owner who rents only through a manager or a booking site needs none. An owner who books guests directly needs one. The exception is a home rented one week or less in each calendar quarter.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>The county's fee.</strong> Horry County adds a hospitality fee on short stays: 3 percent outside city limits and 1.5 percent inside. Cities may add their own. When a manager arranges the stay, the county's page says the manager should collect and pay it.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>A city business license.</strong> The City of Myrtle Beach requires one for every rental property, short-term or long-term.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every tax on a stay is on our <a href="/invest/accommodations-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">accommodations tax page</a>, and the setup steps are on <a href="/invest/str-setup/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">setting up a short-term rental</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want to know who collects each tax on your rental?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the manager's agreement or the booking site you plan to use. We go through who collects and pays each tax with you.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us about the rental taxes</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="the-law"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Contracts and the law">How do I fire a property manager in South Carolina?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Give the notice your agreement asks for. <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t40c057.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">State law</a> adds four rules an owner can use:</p><ul class="pm-rules" role="list"><li><p class="t">A way out after the first term</p><p>An agreement that renews on its own must let either side cancel on 30 days' notice after the first term.</p></li><li><p class="t">Renewal pay on page one</p><p>The agreement must say how the manager is paid. Pay for a future lease renewal must be in underlined capital letters on page one.</p></li><li><p class="t">The deposit list, within 30 days</p><p>Any deduction must be listed in a written notice to the tenant, with any balance. The 30 days run from the latest of three things: the tenancy ends, the tenant hands back the home, and the tenant asks for the deposit.</p></li><li><p class="t">Three times what was wrongly kept</p><p>If the owner misses the 30 days, the tenant can recover three times the amount wrongfully withheld, plus reasonable attorney's fees.</p></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The agreement also may not bind you to list the home for sale with the same firm. The rest of the licensing law is about how a manager's office must run.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The deposit rules bind you as the owner, manager or not. More is on our <a href="/invest/landlord-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">South Carolina landlord rules page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="property-management-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Property management FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are property management fees tax deductible?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Management fees are a rental expense you deduct from rental income on your tax return.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does a property manager need a license in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Managing someone else's property for a fee needs a real estate license. Every licensed manager works under a broker-in-charge or a property manager-in-charge.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can a manager's unlicensed staff negotiate my lease?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Staff without a license may not negotiate a lease, approve an application, or explain the management agreement to you.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does my tenant have to be told who owns the home?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. The tenant must be told in writing, at or before the lease starts, the name and address of the owner or the owner's agent. A manager who signs a lease without that notice takes on the landlord's duties for that lease and receives the tenant's notices and legal papers.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is an HOA management company the same thing?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. A company that runs a homeowners association is a different job. This page is about a manager who rents out your home.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t40c057.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 40-57</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c040.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 27-40</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR lodging tax</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/treasurer/hospitality-fee/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County hospitality fee</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach business licenses</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/publications/p527" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Publication 527</a>, <a href="https://www.hud.gov/helping-americans/fair-housing-act-overview" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD Fair Housing Act</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/assessor/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County assessor</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/microdata.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census microdata</a>. Fees: the fee pages of the 5 managers that publish them; most do not. Owners: our count of county parcels by tax-bill ZIP code. Bookings: AirROI, past year. The $1,600 rent is near the middle for 3-bedroom houses leased in the past two years, with a wide margin. Not legal or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">A key in a lockbox. Photo: Brainy J, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Key_in_lockbox.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty cropped the portrait photo to 4x3, resized it and cut 1x1, 4x3 and 16x9 crops.</div><div role="listitem">Tall oceanfront towers with rows of balconies behind the dune in Myrtle Beach, with more towers lined up along the beach into the distance under a blue sky. Photo: DiscoA340, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hotels_along_the_Grand_Strand_Beachfront.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the photo and cut 1x1, 4x3 and 16x9 crops from its lower part.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/invest-property-management/key-in-a-lockbox-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3rea