+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much do rental programs charge in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"One oceanfront resort's rental desk took 38.6 percent of the rent, plus a monthly health club fee and repairs. In its sample statement the owner kept about 29 cents of each rent dollar. Airbnb takes 15.5 percent from most hosts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Airbnb still charge hosts 3 percent?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Airbnb's 3 percent host fee is being phased out. Airbnb is moving every home host to one fee, and most hosts pay 15.5 percent. Vrbo charges 12 percent."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use Airbnb while I am in the program?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not at the resort whose rules this page shows. Its desk was the only rental agent, and booking your own guests broke the agreement. Leaving took 90 days' notice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays the accommodations tax when the program books the guest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The program, because it takes the payment. If you book a guest yourself, you collect and pay that stay's tax."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does joining a rental program affect my loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For many standard loans, the lender looks at the building, not at whether you join. Many standard loans are not made on any unit in a building run like a hotel. Signs are a front desk, central keys or rules on when owners may stay."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a license to rent out my own condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No real estate license. Anyone paid to list or rent it for you needs one. Inside Myrtle Beach city limits, every rental also needs a city business license."}}]}</script>
