 ## Property management FAQ
 
-### Do I need a property manager for a Myrtle Beach rental?
-No. An owner may manage their own property without a license. A manager makes sense when you live elsewhere, when the building has a rental desk, or when you do not want the calls.
+### Are property management fees tax deductible?
+Yes. Management fees are a rental expense you deduct from rental income on your tax return.
 
-### What license must a property manager have in South Carolina?
-A real estate broker license or a property manager license, and they must work under a broker-in-charge or property manager-in-charge who is responsible for the trust account.
+### Does a property manager need a license in South Carolina?
+Yes. Managing someone else's property for a fee needs a real estate license. Every licensed manager works under a broker-in-charge or a property manager-in-charge.
 
-### Where is my tenant's security deposit kept?
-In the manager's trust account until the lease ends. State law requires it. When the tenant leaves, any deduction must be itemized in writing within 30 days.
+### Can a manager's unlicensed staff negotiate my lease?
+No. Staff without a license may not negotiate a lease, approve an application, or explain the management agreement to you.
 
-### Who pays the accommodations tax when a manager books the guest?
-The manager, on the full booking, because the manager takes the payment. You remit the tax only on stays you book yourself, and then you need a retail license.
+### Does my tenant have to be told who owns the home?
+Yes. The tenant must be told in writing, at or before the lease starts, the name and address of the owner or the owner's agent. A manager who signs a lease without that notice takes on the landlord's duties for that lease and receives the tenant's notices and legal papers.
 
-### Can the management agreement renew automatically?
-Only with a clause that lets either side cancel on 30 days' notice after the first term ends. State law requires that clause.
