-## Can you still use your own unit?
-Under the program, only as the agreement allows. Some agreements cap owner nights. Some require notice to hold dates. Some reserve peak weeks for guests, and some charge the owner a cleaning fee for a personal stay. Self-managing, you block the calendar whenever you want.
-Personal use has a tax limit either way. More than 14 nights a year, or 10 percent of the nights it was rented, and the unit counts as a home for tax. The 14-day rule .
