-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/sell/fsbo/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house without a realtor in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, it is legal. You will still need a licensed South Carolina attorney to close, and you still owe the buyer the state property condition disclosure and, on homes built before 1978, the federal lead paint disclosure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you help FSBO sellers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We coach FSBO sellers for a flat fee: pricing from sold comps, prep, the disclosure, the contract, buyer financing checks, and closing preparation. You do the work and keep the savings. If you hire us to list at any point, the full coaching fee is credited back."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do FSBO homes sell for less?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On national data, yes. The National Association of Realtors' 2025 profile puts the median FSBO sale at 360,000 dollars against 425,000 dollars for agent-listed homes. Part of the gap is that many FSBO sales go to someone the seller already knew, and pre-arranged sales are rarely full-price sales."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What paperwork does a FSBO seller need in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A real purchase contract, the South Carolina Residential Property Condition Disclosure Statement delivered before or at contract signing, the lead paint disclosure for pre-1978 homes, and the closing documents your attorney prepares."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do buyers find FSBO homes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mostly signs, marketplace sites, and word of mouth. Around 88 percent of buyers work with an agent, and agents search the MLS. A home that is not on the MLS is invisible to most of that pool unless you pay a flat-fee broker to place it there."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many people sell FSBO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About 5 percent of national sales in the 2025 NAR profile, the lowest share ever recorded, while 91 percent of sellers used an agent. About one in five FSBO sellers ends up hiring an agent before the home sells."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the hardest part of FSBO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pricing. It is the number one difficulty FSBO sellers report to NAR. Price high and the home sits and takes price cuts. Price low and the loss is immediate and invisible."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will you help me even if I do not buy coaching?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We will prepare your free market analysis either way, so your price is accurate. If you later decide the workload is not worth it, we pick the listing up from wherever you are."}}]}</script>
