ather and less crowds. The winter months of December through February can be quieter but, there are still visitors who come to enjoy the city&#x27;s Christmas and New Year celebrations, and the city&#x27;s other events.</p></div></div><div data-w-tab="Tab 3" class="tab_pane w-tab-pane"><div class="tab_illo-wrapper"><p class="paragraph-38 tabs-content">Myrtle Beach has specific short-term rental regulations in place to ensure the safety and comfort of guests. These include obtaining a short-term rental permit, adhering to zoning and parking regulations and paying a transient lodging tax. Hosts are also required to provide certain safety features such as smoke detectors and emergency evacuation plans.</p></div></div><div data-w-tab="Tab 4" class="tab_pane w-tab-pane"><div class="tab_lilo-wrapper"><p class="paragraph-38 tabs-content">Managing an Airbnb property in Myrtle Beach can be challenging due to the high competition and the need to maintain the property&#x27;s cleanliness and upkeep. A professional property manager can help by handling the day-to-day operations such as cleaning, maintenance, and guest communication. They can also assist in pricing, marketing, and booking to help increase occupancy rates.</p></div></div><div data-w-tab="Tab 5" class="tab_pane w-tab-pane"><div class="tab_lilo-wrapper"><p class="paragraph-38 tabs-content">The most sought-after amenities and locations in Myrtle Beach for Airbnb rentals include properties with beachfront access, private outdoor spaces, and proximity to downtown Myrtle Beach and the beach. Properties with views of the Atlantic Ocean are also highly desirable. Additionally, locations near golf courses and marinas are popular with guests looking to enjoy the city&#x27;s outdoor attractions.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="w-embed"><style>
