-column"><div class="fusion-text fusion-text-19" style="--awb-font-size:16px;--awb-line-height:25px;--awb-text-color:#515151;"><p>Doug Dale is the Co-founder, Chief Real Estate Investment Officer, and Head of Institutional at PURE HomeRiver, the nation’s largest third-party property management company for single-family rental (SFR) properties. He leads the company’s institutional strategy, joint ventures, and investment management platform, overseeing relationships with private equity firms, asset managers, and large-scale residential investors nationwide.</p>
+<p>Doug leads the fundraising and management of PURE HomeRiver’s joint venture platform, including the company’s first institutional joint venture and the recent launch of its second joint venture. Over his career, he has deployed more than $5 billion into the single-family rental sector and overseen the acquisition and operation of more than ten thousand residential properties.</p>
+<p>An experienced entrepreneur and operator, prior to co-founding HomeRiver Group, Doug co-founded one of the nation’s largest single-family investment firms and co-founded a staffing firm that grew to over 1,000 employees and serviced Fortune 500 companies before its sale. His experience spans acquisitions, underwriting, asset management, renovations, and portfolio operations across institutional and retail platforms. Doug graduated with honors from Butler University and lives in Carmel Indiana with his wife and their two sons.</p>
