+Accommodations
+Accommodations Tax applies to sleeping accommodations of any kind that are rented to guests for less than 90 consecutive days.
+What is Accommodations Tax?
+Accommodations can include rooms or spaces in your own home, hotels, condos, campgrounds, boarding houses, mobile home parks, or any other similar lodgings.
+Need help?
+Phone:
+​803-898-5970
+Email:
+AccommodationsTax@dor.sc.gov
+General Inquiries Only
+Accommodations are subject to:
+5% Sales Tax​
+2% Accommodations Tax
+Any local Sales & Use Tax that is collected on behalf of counties by the SCDOR.​
+​South Carolina Accommodations tax rates by Municipality ​​​​(
+ST-575
+)​
+South Carolina Municipality codes (
+ST-604
+)
+Check out our helpful chart
+if you still​ aren't sure if you need to pay Accommodations Tax.
+Which accommodations are not subject to the tax?
+Accommodations Tax does not apply to:
+The lease or rental of accommodations supplied to the same person for a period of 90 continuous days​
+A facility with six or fewer bedrooms, provided that:
+​​the facility is on the same premises where the owner or operator lives at the time the other rooms are rented,
+and
+the owner or operator does not use a rental agency or online travel company to rent rooms.
+Accommodations provided to foreign diplomats
+Accommodations billed directly to federal government agencies, the American Red Cross, federal credit unions, or charitable children's hospitals.
+For more information on Sales Tax exemptions and exclusions, refer to
+Chapter 11
+of the
+SCDOR's Sales and Use Tax Manual
+.
+How is Accommodations Tax distributed back to cities and counties?​
+The 2% portion of the Accommodations Tax is distributed back to cities and counties using a formula based on point of sale.
+A municipality receiving more than $50,000 in Accommodations Tax revenue must appoint an advisory committee to recommend to the municipality’s Council how the money is spent. The Council can then accept, reject, or modify the recommendations.
+The first $25,000 of the Accommodations Tax distribution is deposited into the local governments’ general funds. Of the balance, 30% must be allocated to a special fund for the exclusive use of tourism advertising and promotion, and the remaining balance must be used for tourism-related expenditures.
+Local governments can charge up to an additional 3% in Accommodations Tax. The proceeds must be used for tourism-related projects and programs as defined in
+SC Code Section 6-1-530
+.
+Who should I contact for more information on ​local accommodations tax?​
+Many counties and municipalities in South Carolina also impose local accommodations taxes that are not administered by the ​SCDOR. Please
+contact the county or municipal office where your rental property is located
+to determine what additional local taxes you are required to rep​ort to that jurisdiction.
+Licensing
+If you are directly booking short-term rentals, you must have a
+Retail License
+to file and pay Accommodations Tax.
+A Retail License is not required if you rent a room or space for no more than one week each calendar quarter—but you are required to file and pay the tax annually.
+I have multiple vacation rental properties. Can I use one Retail License for all locations?
+If you are a property owner with more than one location that provides short term accommodations, you must have a
+Retail License​
+for each location. ​As the property owner you are responsible for collecting and paying Accommodations Tax for the rentals that you booked without the service of the property management or online travel company.
+Do I need a Retail License if I use a property management or online travel company to ren​t my property?
+No, if you rent your property exclusively through a property management or online travel company that is reserving rooms and accepting payment for booking, they are responsible for remitting the tax for the full amount of the booking. Therefore, you are not required to have a Retail License with South Carolina.
+How do I close a Business Tax account?
+You have two options for closing your account:
+Log in to
+MyDORWAY
+, then select the
+More
+tab, and click
+Close a Tax Account
+to get started.
+or
+Close your account on your final tax return by checking “Has the business been permanently closed?” and typing in the closed date.
+How to file and pay
+Accommodations taxpayers must file and pay all Accommodations taxes electronically.
+See filing requirements if you have multiple locations
+Accommodations taxpayers who file returns for multiple locations are required to submit additional location-specific information electronically on MyDORWAY when filing their return.
+WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW
+If you only own one location or rental unit,
+meaning you only file an Accommodations Tax return for that property, this requirement does
+not
+apply to you.
+If you are a property owner with more than one location
+that provides short term rentals, you must have a Retail License for each location but are not required to submit additional information.
+If you are a property management company who rents multiple properties
+that are individually owned, you must upload the following information for each location through MyDORWAY with each Accommodations Tax return (
+failure to submit this information will result in a penalty
+):​
+​The location address, including count​y and municipality
+The net taxable sales at each location
+The location-specific information must be reported to the SCDOR through a new upload tool on
+MyDORWAY
+.
+The report is due with your monthly return​.
+Failure to submit the required information will result in a penalty.
+HOW TO FILE AND PAY
+Collect and upload the required location-specific information for each of your locations.
+The link to upload your list of locations will be available after you file your first return that includes the multiple locations:
+​On the
+Accounts
+tab, next to your
+Accommodations Tax
+account, select
+Upload Accommodations List of Locations
+(as shown below):
+From here you will have the option to either
+manually input your location entries
+or
+download an Excel template and upload the file
+once it is completed.
+After you have completed your entries or uploaded your Excel file, click
+Submit
+.
+QUESTIONS? WE’RE HERE TO HELP
+Send us a web message from your MyDORWAY account:
+Log in
+and go to the
+More
+tab and click
+Send SCDOR a Message
+under
+Correspondence
+Create a MyDORWAY account if you do not already have one. Visit
+dor.sc.gov/MyDORWAY​
+to learn more and get started.
+File and pay on ​​MyDORWAY
+​
+MyDORWAY
+​
+is the preferred way to securely file taxes and make payments using a credit card or electronic check (ACH Debit or Electronic Funds Withdrawal).
+Need a MyDORWAY account?​
+Sign up
